Exp34 result: REJECTED under the frozen DAY_WEIGHTED whole-ISO-week criterion. Sample 349 completed broker-days across 71 ISO weeks; TRAIN 205/42, VALIDATION 72/14, TEST 72/15. TRAIN k_location=+0.393791943. Association weakened in Validation and reversed in Test. Validation Brier gain -0.000513171 CI[-0.009102143,+0.008945783], LogLoss -0.001151627 CI[-0.018083768,+0.017444149]. Test Brier gain -0.011261615 CI[-0.018107754,-0.004310170], LogLoss -0.022941845 CI[-0.037240355,-0.008536985]. Strict pass=False. Exp27 untouched. Runtime promotion NONE.

Exp35 frozen methodological checkpoint: temporal-stability audit only, no new predictive feature and no rescue of Exp31-Exp34. Historical rows remain strictly before 2026-08-13 00:00 BRT. Reconstruct exact already-frozen Track-B coordinates Streak2, PrevCompress/RangeRatio20, PrevEfficiency, PrevAlignedPosition20 and their original targets. Partition ordered eligible ISO weeks into exactly six contiguous approximately equal eras. Per era report unconditional continuation/expansion rates; Streak2 continuation difference; Spearman PrevEfficiency vs continuation; Spearman PrevAlignedPosition20 vs continuation; PrevCompress expansion difference; and feature distributions. Use whole-ISO-week bootstrap within each era for descriptive 95% intervals. No model promotion, no threshold/window search, no reopening rejected features. If target rates are stable but conditional associations repeatedly change sign, classify simple first-order Track-B conditional structure as temporally unstable/regime-sensitive. If target rates also vary materially, record base-rate nonstationarity as an additional concern. Any next predictive family must wait until this checkpoint is interpreted. Exp27 untouched. Runtime promotion NONE.

Exp35 implementation note: first execution aborted during ERA2 bootstrap with IndexError because per-era DataFrame labels were not reset before being used as positional NumPy indices. ERA1 output is partial descriptive audit only and is not an Exp35 verdict. Scientific contract, six eras, reconstructed features, targets, bootstrap design, and interpretation rules remain unchanged. Correction: bootstrap_era now resets cont/exp indices locally before building per-week positional index arrays. No predictive fit or promotion decision occurred before the abort.

Exp35 result — Track B temporal-stability audit: COMPLETED. Historical sample: 349 common continuation days, 348 exact Exp32 expansion days, 71 ISO weeks partitioned into six frozen contiguous eras (12/12/12/12/12/11 weeks). Continuation base rate ranged 33.93% to 50.82% (16.89 pp span); expansion base rate ranged 43.64% to 52.54% (8.91 pp span). Conditional effect signs were unstable across eras: Streak2Diff [+,+,+,+,-,-], EfficiencySpearman [+,-,+,-,-,-], LocationSpearman [-,+,+,+,+,-], PrevCompressDiff [-,+,-,-,-,+]. Notable descriptive whole-week bootstrap exclusions of zero occurred in ERA3 EfficiencySpearman +0.2328 CI[+0.0300,+0.4304], ERA4 PrevCompressDiff -0.3542 CI[-0.6667,-0.0167], and ERA6 Streak2Diff -0.3462 CI[-0.5536,-0.1634]. Feature distributions moved only moderately relative to the repeated sign reversals: PrevEfficiency era means ~0.4415-0.5077; PrevAlignedPosition20 means ~+0.1131 to +0.2531; PrevCompress incidence ~45.76%-57.38%; Streak2 incidence ~33.93%-50.00%. Interpretation before Exp36: descriptive sign instability/regime-sensitivity hypothesis only; this did NOT identify a regime variable or rescue Exp31-Exp34. Simple first-order Track-B feature search paused. Exp27 untouched. Runtime promotion NONE.

Exp36 frozen methodological checkpoint — whole-ISO-week temporal-exchangeability test. Purpose: quantify whether the era-to-era heterogeneity seen in Exp35 is larger than expected if ISO weeks were exchangeable over time, without introducing any new predictive feature or reopening rejected hypotheses. Reconstruct exactly the Exp35 common continuation sample and exact Exp32 expansion sample, the same four frozen conditional statistics (Streak2Diff, EfficiencySpearman, LocationSpearman, PrevCompressDiff), and the two unconditional target rates. Keep the exact six era sizes in weeks (12/12/12/12/12/11). Define one frozen heterogeneity statistic per quantity: day-count-weighted squared deviation of each era estimate from the corresponding all-history estimate, divided by total days. Generate 10,000 whole-week random reallocations to six pseudo-eras preserving the exact era week counts; each ISO week moves as an indivisible block and each permutation uses the same week allocation for all diagnostics. For each quantity report H_observed, permutation median, permutation 95th percentile, and p_perm=P(H_perm>=H_observed). This is a stationarity/exchangeability diagnostic only. No coefficient fitting, no model scoring, no threshold/window search, no feature selection, no promotion, no post-hoc era count changes. If multiple frozen conditional quantities reject week-exchangeability while feature distributions remain broadly similar, strengthen TEMPORAL_CONDITIONAL_INSTABILITY; if only base rates reject, prioritize target/base-rate drift; if neither rejects, downgrade Exp35 sign flips toward sampling variability. Exp27 untouched. Runtime promotion NONE.

Exp36 result — COMPLETED / NO REJECTION OF WHOLE-WEEK TEMPORAL EXCHANGEABILITY. Exact sample reproduced: 349 common continuation days, 348 expansion days, 71 ISO weeks, era sizes 12/12/12/12/12/11. None of the six frozen quantities rejected at p_perm<0.05. ContinuationBaseRate Hobs=0.002995300, Perm95=0.007274850, p=49.08%; Streak2Diff Hobs=0.026564661, Perm95=0.031199491, p=9.68%; EfficiencySpearman Hobs=0.022886886, Perm95=0.029593372, p=13.84%; LocationSpearman Hobs=0.018314378, Perm95=0.035250953, p=37.53%; ExpansionBaseRate Hobs=0.001057955, Perm95=0.013501715, p=97.74%; PrevCompressDiff Hobs=0.028190315, Perm95=0.050157271, p=31.65%. Frozen summary: conditional rejections 0/4; base-rate rejections 0/2. Therefore the Exp35 era sign flips and base-rate spans must be downgraded toward finite-sample/week-allocation variability under this frozen diagnostic; TEMPORAL_CONDITIONAL_INSTABILITY is NOT statistically strengthened and no regime-model justification follows from Exp35/36. Streak2 and Efficiency are the closest conditional quantities to the rejection boundary but remain non-rejections and cannot be cherry-picked or rescued. Exp31-Exp34 remain rejected. Exp27 untouched. Runtime promotion NONE.

Exp37 pre-run methodological correction: the initially drafted NULL P(continue)=0.5 was withdrawn before execution because 0.5 implicitly assumes balanced marginal UP/DOWN probability; with directional marginal imbalance, an independent-sign process need not have P(same sign)=0.5. No Exp37 data were scored under that draft.

Exp37 frozen redesigned Track-B baseline — first-order daily sign Markov dependence versus marginal-direction independence. This is a target-process dependence audit, not a new feature search. Use completed M5 broker-days strictly before 2026-08-13 00:00 BRT; drop first/last file-edge broker-days; day_sign=sign(Close-Open); target y_up_d=1 iff day_sign_d=+1; require current and prior day_sign non-zero. Split whole eligible ISO weeks chronologically 60/20/20 and freeze assignments before scoring. NULL fits exactly one TRAIN-only marginal probability pi_up=P_TRAIN(day_sign=UP) and predicts pi_up for every Validation/Test day, ignoring prior sign. MARKOV1 fits exactly two TRAIN-only transition probabilities q_up_after_up=P_TRAIN(curr UP|prev UP) and q_up_after_down=P_TRAIN(curr UP|prev DOWN); OOS prediction chooses the corresponding frozen probability using only the observed prior completed-day sign. No smoothing, no UP/DOWN post-hoc rescue, no rolling/refit, no extra features. Primary estimand=DAY_WEIGHTED; uncertainty=whole-ISO-week bootstrap preserving day weights. Primary comparison MARKOV1 over NULL uses binary Brier and LogLoss gain; survival requires both gain CI95>0 in BOTH Validation and Test. Secondary diagnostics report the frozen TRAIN transition matrix and observed OOS transition rates only; they cannot rescue primary failure. If MARKOV1 fails, close static first-order daily-sign dependence beyond marginal directional imbalance under this historical contract. If it survives, preserve only as historical exploratory baseline requiring future validation; do not combine with Exp31-Exp34. Exp27 untouched. Runtime promotion NONE.

Exp37 result — REJECTED under the frozen DAY_WEIGHTED whole-ISO-week criterion. Exact sample: 368 eligible completed broker-days across 74 ISO weeks; TRAIN 219/44, VALIDATION 77/15, TEST 72/15. Marginal UP rate moved 57.08% TRAIN -> 54.55% VALIDATION -> 48.61% TEST. Frozen TRAIN transition kernel: P(UP|prevUP)=0.507936508, P(UP|prevDOWN)=0.655913978, difference=-0.147977471. The descriptive anti-persistence sign remained negative OOS but attenuated: -0.1000 in VALIDATION and -0.0564 in TEST. MARKOV1-over-NULL point gains were positive in VALIDATION (Brier +0.001665092, LogLoss +0.003171781) but both whole-week CI95 crossed zero; in TEST gains were negative (Brier -0.003712761, LogLoss -0.008447762) with CI95 also crossing zero. Strict pass=False. Interpretation: a weak descriptive anti-persistence tendency may exist, but the frozen static first-order daily-sign probability kernel is not transportable enough to beat the marginal-direction null under the preregistered historical OOS contract. No shrinkage, calibration, rolling/refit, asymmetric transition rescue, higher-lag rescue, or combination with Exp31-Exp34 is allowed. Exp31-Exp34 remain rejected; Exp35/36 do not justify a regime model. Track B daily-direction first-order program is PAUSED/CLOSED pending materially more independent daily history or a separately preregistered redesign of target/horizon; no Exp38 predictive feature test is opened from this result. Exp27 untouched. Runtime promotion NONE.
